    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a4836cca1208c95",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ce39cdc1da64e92f5a2c721fd6d383143c7c11a93a545add9a4a560c05edb171",
      "text": "Land in Lima and settle in at your hotel, then head out to explore the historic centre, a UNESCO World Heritage Site full of colonial gems. Start at the Convent of Santo Domingo, built when Lima was founded, where the University of San Marcos, one of the oldest in the Americas, began; it has the country’s oldest wooden choir stalls and a library of 25,000 books, some dating back to the 1500s. The remains of three of Peru’s most revered saints, Saint Martin de Porres, Saint Juan Macías and Saint Rose of Lima, rest here.\n\nCross the Plaza Mayor, past the Government Palace and City Hall, and step into the Cathedral, one of Lima’s true colonial treasures. To close the day, leave the old town for the Larco Museum, where gold artefacts, ancient textiles and the museum’s famous erotic ceramics offer a window into how Peru’s earliest cultures saw the world, with access to the museum’s storage galleries, a rare look at pieces not usually on display.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1XrZzfxaD87HpTT-eN2AroxoaHB_haPhZ",
        "documentSha256": "90d9d277cfc4f1997307081e08ca6496b6cbe32f9f53f5179fe064857a36b8be",
